course: dictionary
lesson: 6580
title: Nineteen: more than a number
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nineteen is a number. You can write it as 19, and it is ten and nine put together. It is also one less than twenty.
explain: You use nineteen to count things, like 19 pages in a book or 19 steps up a hill. You also use it to say an age: a person who is nineteen is in their late teens.
explain: Context helps you read it. «Tutankhamun became pharaoh as a boy of about nine and died at about nineteen.» The word nineteen here is an age, not a sum, so read the words around it to tell which sense is meant.
fact: Nineteen is the number 19, which is ten and nine.
fact: Nineteen is one less than twenty.
fact: 19 is a prime number, because only 1 and 19 divide into it exactly.
fact: A person who is nineteen is in their late teens.
fact: «Nineteen to the dozen» is a UK saying that means talking very fast.
exercise: What number is written as 19? | *Nineteen | Ninety | Twenty-one | Eleven
exercise: «Tutankhamun ... died at about nineteen.» About what age did he die? | Nine | Twenty-nine | *Nineteen | Twelve
exercise: Which two numbers add up to nineteen? | *Ten and nine | Five and five | Ten and ten | Twelve and six
test: What is one less than twenty? | *Nineteen | Twenty-one | Eighteen | Ten
test: Nadia says «nineteen to the dozen» means talking very quietly. Is she right? | It means exactly nineteen dozen eggs | It means a long walk | *No, it means talking very fast | Yes, it means talking very quietly
exam: A person who is nineteen is in which stage of life? | Their seventies | Their early childhood | *Their late teens | Their first year at school
